// #taxon[Taxon]
#title[Models of HoTT]

there are *lots* of categorical models of dependent types
- Categorical models with families: CwF
- Natural models (see Awodey)
- Categrogies with attributes: CwA
- Comprehensible categories
- Display map categories
- B C systems

Intetional Identity Types correspond to  weak factorization systems.

See https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/weak+factorization+system

- some people also look at weak factorization systems

To convice a mathematician that HoTT is actually synthetical homotopy theory,
refer them to https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.1211.2851 .
- they use kan fibrations and kan complexes

With HoTT we talk about higher structures, so we need to think about what
higher category theory should be.

Idea: Replace equalities with higher morphisms
- 0-cells become objects
- 1-cells morphisms
- ...


